id: clock_manager_perpll1_runtime_config
label: Clock Manager PERPLL1 Runtime Configuration
package: platform_core
description: >
  Marks PERPLL1 as runtime-configurable. When this component is present,
  PERPLL1 stops being a fixed compile-time clock source: its frequency can
  be reprogrammed at runtime through the Clock Manager runtime configuration
  APIs, typically by the I2S driver so that it can produce an exact audio
  sample rate.

  Because reprogramming PERPLL1 affects every Clock Branch fed by it, adding
  this component reserves PERPLL1 for I2S0CLK. The Clock Manager validation
  warns if any other Clock Branch is configured to use PERPLL1.
category: Services|Clock Manager
quality: evaluation
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: Zlib
provides:
- name: clock_manager_perpll1_runtime_config
requires:
- name: device_series_3
- name: device_has_perpll1
template_contribution:
- name: component_catalog
  value: clock_manager_perpll1_runtime_config
root_path: platform_core
